12
00:51:39,130 --> 00:51:45,130
50 First Dates is a 2004 American romantic comedy film directed by Peter Segal and starring Adam Sandler and Drew
Barrymore, with Rob Schneider, Sean Astin, Lusia Strus, Blake Clark, and Dan Aykroyd in supporting roles.

13
00:55:57,391 --> 00:56:03,391
It follows the story of Henry Roth, a womanizing marine veterinarian
who falls for an art teacher named Lucy Whitmore.

14
01:00:15,652 --> 01:00:21,652
When he discovers she has amnesia, and forgets him when she falls
asleep, he resolves to win her over again each new day.

15
01:04:33,913 --> 01:04:39,913
Most of the film was shot on location in Oahu, Hawaii, on
the Windward side and the North Shore.

16
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
Sandler and Barrymore won an MTV Movie Award for Best On-Screen Team.

17
01:13:10,434 --> 01:13:16,434
The film received mixed reviews but was a commercial success.

18
01:17:28,695 --> 01:17:34,695
It was later remade in India as Satyabhama (2007, in Telugu) and as Ormayundo Ee Mukham (2014, in Malayalam), in Japan as
50 First Kisses (2018), in Iran as Chap dast (2005), and in Mexico as Como si fuera la primera vez (2019).

19
01:21:46,956 --> 01:21:52,956
The film marked the second collaboration between Sandler and Barrymore, after The
Wedding Singer and before Blended (both directed by Frank Coraci).

20
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
During the end credits, it featured a dedication to the memory of Sandler's father
Stanley, who had died at the age of 68 from lung cancer on September 9, 2003.

21
01:30:23,478 --> 01:30:29,478
The film explores themes of amnesia, hawaii, romcom, deception, womanizer.

22
01:34:41,739 --> 01:34:47,739
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
